  "summary": "The Woodlands Township approved 30 new Flock Safety ALPR cameras as part of its 2026 budget, at $109,500 the first year and $90,000 annually thereafter. The Montgomery County Sheriff's Office plans to install them by summer, citing investigative and deterrent value, while the ACLU of Texas has raised privacy concerns.",
